# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  fastlane/.env.example — TEMPLATE, SAFE TO COMMIT
#
#  Setup:
#    cp fastlane/.env.example fastlane/.env
#    # Fill in your actual values
#
#  The .env file is gitignored — NEVER commit .env
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  App Store Connect API Key (iOS)                           │
# │                                                             │
# │  Create at: App Store Connect → Users and Access           │
# │             → Integrations → App Store Connect API          │
# │  Required role: App Manager or Developer                   │
# │                                                             │
# │  WHY API Key instead of App-Specific Password:             │
# │  App-Specific Password requires interactive 2FA →          │
# │  CI hangs waiting for OTP with no one to enter it.        │
# │  API Key = service account, not blocked by 2FA.           │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# Key ID — 10 characters, e.g. AB12CD34EF
# Find at: App Store Connect → API Keys → copy "Key ID"
ASC_KEY_ID=XXXXXXXXXX

# Issuer ID — UUID format, found on the same API Keys page (at the top)
ASC_ISSUER_ID=xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx

# Contents of the .p8 file — download once when creating the key
# Can paste the full block, use \n for newlines:
#   ASC_KEY_CONTENT=-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nXXXXXX\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----
# Or use a file path to the .p8 (use key_filepath instead of key_content in app_store_connect_api_key)
ASC_KEY_CONTENT=-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nXXXXXXXXXXXX\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  Apple Developer Account                                   │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# Apple ID email registered with Apple Developer Program
APPLE_ID=your@email.com

# Team ID — 10 characters (letters + numbers)
# Find at: developer.apple.com → Account → Membership → Team ID
TEAM_ID=XXXXXXXXXX

# Bundle Identifier — must match the App ID in Apple Developer Portal
# e.g. com.yourcompany.yourapp
APP_IDENTIFIER=com.demo_app

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  Match — Code Signing (iOS certificates + profiles)        │
# │                                                             │
# │  Setup: create a separate private repo to store certs      │
# │  (encrypted), e.g. github.com/your-org/ios-certs          │
# │  Then run: bundle exec fastlane ios sync_certs             │
# │                                                             │
# │  WHY match (instead of managing certs manually):           │
# │  - All certs are encrypted and stored centrally            │
# │  - New team member: run sync_certs and they're ready       │
# │  - No more "cert only on machine A" → team can't build     │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# URL of the cert repo (HTTPS)
# e.g. https://github.com/your-org/ios-certs.git
MATCH_GIT_URL=https://github.com/your-org/ios-certs.git

# GitHub Personal Access Token — needs repo scope (read + write)
# Create at: github.com → Settings → Developer settings
#            → Personal access tokens → Tokens (classic) → Generate
# Required scopes: repo (full control of private repositories)
MATCH_GIT_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Password to encrypt/decrypt certs in the match repo
# All team members and CI must use the same password
# Store this password securely (1Password, LastPass, etc.)
MATCH_PASSWORD=your_match_encryption_password

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  Android Signing                                            │
# │                                                             │
# │  Create release keystore (one time only):                  │
# │  keytool -genkey -v \                                      │
# │    -keystore release.keystore \                            │
# │    -alias <alias-name> \                                   │
# │    -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000               │
# │                                                             │
# │  CRITICAL: Back up keystore + passwords in multiple places!│
# │  Losing the keystore = unable to update app on Play Store. │
# │  Google CANNOT recover it.                                 │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# Absolute path to the .keystore file
# e.g. /Users/antonio/certs/demo_app_release.keystore
ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PATH=/path/to/release.keystore

# Alias you set when creating the keystore (see -alias in the keytool command above)
ANDROID_KEYSTORE_ALIAS=your-key-alias

# Store password (set when creating the keystore)
ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=your-store-password

# Key password (set when creating the keystore, may be the same as store password)
ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD=your-key-password

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  Google Play (Android upload)                              │
# │                                                             │
# │  Setup service account:                                    │
# │  1. Google Cloud Console → APIs → Google Play Android      │
# │     Developer API → Enable                                 │
# │  2. Create Service Account → download JSON key             │
# │  3. Google Play Console → Setup → API Access               │
# │     → Grant access to service account (Release Manager)   │
# │                                                             │
# │  NOTE: First upload must be done manually via Play Console!│
# │  supply (fastlane) only works from the second upload on.  │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# Absolute path to the service account JSON key file
GOOGLE_PLAY_JSON_KEY_PATH=/path/to/google-play-key.json

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  Release Configuration                                      │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# Version name displayed to users (semantic versioning)
# e.g. 1.2.3
APP_VERSION=1.0.0

# Android staged rollout percentage (used by the production lane)
# 0.1 = 10%, 0.25 = 25%, 0.5 = 50%, 1.0 = 100%
# Start small, increase gradually after confirming no crashes
ROLLOUT_PERCENTAGE=0.1

# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  Slack Notifications (optional)                            │
# │                                                             │
# │  Create an Incoming Webhook:                               │
# │  api.slack.com → Your Apps → Create App                   │
# │  → Incoming Webhooks → Activate → Add to Workspace        │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# Leave blank to disable Slack notifications
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXXXX/XXXXX/XXXXX
